@startuml SI4735_Signal_Flow
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
skinparam activityBorderColor #1565C0
skinparam shadowing false

title SI4735 — FM Signal Processing Flow

|RF Front-End|
start
:Receive FM signal\n(64–108 MHz);
:Low Noise Amplifier (LNA)\nAmplify weak RF signal;
:Mixer + Local Oscillator\nDown-convert to IF;
:IF Filter\nReject adjacent channels;

|ADC|
:Analog-to-Digital Conversion\nDigitise IF signal;

|DSP Core|
:FM Demodulation\n(Frequency Discriminator);

fork
  :Channel Filter\nProgrammable bandwidth\n(60/84/110/150 kHz);
  :AGC Processing\nAdjust digital gain\n(attack/decay rates);
fork again
  :RDS Extraction\n57 kHz subcarrier\nDecode PS, RT, PTY, CT;
fork again
  :AFC Loop\nTrack carrier drift\nCorrect frequency offset;
end fork

:Stereo MPX Decoding\n19 kHz pilot detection\nL+R / L-R separation;

:Stereo Blend\nMono ↔ Stereo transition\nbased on RSSI/SNR;

|DAC|
:Digital-to-Analog Conversion;

|Audio Output|
:Left Channel (LOUT);
:Right Channel (ROUT);
stop

note right
  **Signal Quality Metrics**
  Available at any point:
  • RSSI (dBμV)
  • SNR (dB)
  • Multipath level
  • Frequency offset
  • Valid channel flag
end note

@enduml
